ence Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-803216","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"With AI-based voice cloning tools becoming more accessible to designers, we deem it imperative to understand their paralinguistic capabilities, limitations and cultures. Paralinguistics as a feld of study is concerned with how you say something rather than what you say, and new AI-based statistical voice synthesis tools difer signifcantly from previous methods. As such, they require asking novel questions and provoking new thoughts. This paper contributes by analyzing and evaluating various voice cloning platforms by looking at how they describe their own ability to produce three diferent paralinguistic elements: laughter, stuttering and pacing. We focus on text-to-speech and hybrid approaches to voice cloning, and follow up our analyses by attempting to produce these three paralinguistic elements using the voice cloning platform ElevenLabs’ voice synthesis tools. Conclusively, we draw on our results to pose questions for further investigation into what kinds of AI paralinguistic cultures can and should be designed.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Ada Ada, Ada","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S02-084.47-822879"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["AI","Paralinguistics","Speech synthesis"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"cultures of the ai paralinguistic in voice cloning tools","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3663708","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-084.47-822879","identifier":[{"id":"85198902750","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-98a5d29e-d62c-4537-8056-03005d789706","ku-5a8fab7b-4ec9-46de-92ca-593a649c9f3e"],"keyword":["AI","paralinguistics","speech synthesis","voice cloning"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-7B449B6606D2F313ADC07348E8265D0C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3663708","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Arts and Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Ada","key":"adaadapau","last":"Ada Ada","name":"Ada Ada, Ada","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ada Ada","key":"adapau","last":"Ada","name":"Ada, Ada Ada","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3663708","pages":"249-252","status":"p","title":"Companion Publication of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference (DIS '24 Companion)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198902750"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-98a5d29e-d62c-4537-8056-03005d789706","ku-5a8fab7b-4ec9-46de-92ca-593a649c9f3e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Cultures of the AI paralinguistic in voice cloning tools.","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-084.47-822879","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Computing devices commonly act as tools, extending our abilities and shaping how we interact with the world. We investigate one such tool, the calculator, which helps with arithmetic, but also commonly offers specialized functions for conversions, formulas, or graphing. Through an analysis of calculator apps and use cases, we describe limitations of current calculators. Crucially, calculator apps remain detached from tasks, motivating us to explore how to more closely integrate calculation with the world through augmented reality (AR). AR calculators can directly use measurements and numbers from the world in calculations as well as display results of calculations in the world. We provide a conceptual account of calculation in AR, as well as video prototypes that concretize the concept across different scenarios. These examples demonstrate how moving tools like the calculator to AR offers tighter task integration and reduces the work required in translating between the world and computational tools.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Pohl, Henning","Hornbæk, Kasper"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-735954"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-01","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Augmented reality","Concept","Mobile interaction","Tool use","Video prototyping","calculator"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"integrated calculators moving calculation into the world","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661523","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-735954","identifier":[{"id":"85200407100","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-58291775-8c19-4636-8efa-e139eddca3fc"],"keyword":["augmented reality","calculator","concept","mobile interaction","tool use","video prototyping"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-6D82CFA00A958417D6D2B30B2E35E86D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/753424620/Pohl2024DIS.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661523","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Henning","key":"pohlpau","last":"Pohl","locid":"4f6de337-0278-4daa-9d35-771a790c66a8","name":"Pohl, Henning","orcid":"0000-0002-1420-4309","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Kasper","key":"hornbækpau","last":"Hornbæk","name":"Hornbæk, Kasper","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661523","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"343-355","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"DIS '24: Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200407100"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-58291775-8c19-4636-8efa-e139eddca3fc"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"Integrated Calculators : Moving Calculation into the World","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-735954","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Individuals are increasingly interested in and responsible for assessing their own health. This study evaluates a fctional AI dermatologist for assistance in the self-assessment of moles. Building on the Signalling Theory, we tested the efect of textual descriptions provided by a virtual dermatologist, as manipulated across ‘Ability’, ‘Integrity,’ and ‘Benevolence’, along with the clinical assessment, ‘benign’ or ‘malignant’, afect users’ trust in the aforementioned trust pillars. Our study (N = 40) follows a 2 (Ability low/high) × 2 (Integrity low/high) × 2 (Benevolence low/high) × 2 (mole assessment benign/malignant) within-subject factorial design. Our results demonstrate that we can successfully infuence perceptions of ability and benevolence by manipulating the corresponding aspects of trust but not perceived integrity. Further, in the case of a malignant assessment, participants’ perception of trust increased across all aspects. Our results provide insights into the design of AI support systems for sensitive use cases, such as clinical self-assessments.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Als, Naja Kathrine Kollerup","Wester, Joel","Skov, Mikael B.","van Berkel, Niels"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-771128"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Signalling theory","Trust"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"how can i signal you to trust me investigating ai trust signalling in clinical self assessments","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661612","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-771128","identifier":[{"id":"85200372707","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d2a53070-4a8e-48b2-a6a0-ad8411615ff5"],"keyword":["AI Self-Assessment Tools","Human-AI Trust Building","Signalling theory","Trust"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-DE216D02C0581CB4FDA08E44763AA179"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661612","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/753239239/3643834.3661612.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Naja Kathrine","key":"kolleruppau","last":"Kollerup","locid":"df3c9179-c842-42c2-a1e5-ae30b03f72b2","name":"Als, Naja Kathrine Kollerup","name_org":"Kollerup, Naja Kathrine","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Joel","key":"westerpau","last":"Wester","locid":"db375504-2a91-46a8-b60e-07e6cb8e267d","name":"Wester, Joel","orcid":"0000-0001-6332-9493","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Mikael B.","key":"skovpau","last":"Skov","locid":"c82c4a8d-1612-4218-b5ab-35e729748eb8","name":"Skov, Mikael B.","orcid":"0000-0003-4488-5683","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"vanberkelpau","last":"van Berkel","locid":"4088b4e4-37e9-42fe-8cdc-43ae859a7cdb","name":"van Berkel, Niels","orcid":"0000-0001-5106-7692","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapedh","last":"Vallgårda","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jönssonpedh","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Li","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661612","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"525-540","place":"Copenhagen Denmark","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200372707"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d2a53070-4a8e-48b2-a6a0-ad8411615ff5"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University"],"title":"How Can I Signal You To Trust Me : Investigating AI Trust Signalling in Clinical Self-Assessments","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-771128","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Research through Design is centered on making things, services and systems as a way to construct knowledge. At the same time, the act of making happens behind-the-scenes, often overlooked, outsourced or rushed through. We would like to propose a one-day workshop of making at DIS. Specifically, we propose the making of samplers as a site for constructing a shared space to contemplate the interplay of memory and imagination in design research, inspired by traditional needlework samplers as well as modern subversive stitchwork [24]. By making together, we aim to take time to consider our personal and collective commitments and stance within and outside our roles as design researchers.","author_count":16,"contributors":["Andersen, Kristina","Goveia Da Rocha, Bruna","Devendorf, Laura","Vasconcelos, Elvia","Jones, Lee","Posch, Irene","Reddy, Anuradha Venugopal","Kelliher, Aisling","Fuchsberger, Verena","Hansen, Lone Koefoed","Sandry, Etta"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752628"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Austria","Canada","Netherlands","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology","Queen's University Kingston","University of Art and Industrial Design Linz","University of Colorado Boulder","University of Salzburg","University of Southern California"],"keyword":["Crafting","Critical making","Making","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"memoirs for the future imaginations of the past crafting samplers for intent and commitment","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3658406","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752628","identifier":[{"id":"85198901014","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-146f9ce8-8389-4bf3-9223-3d4dead9340e"],"keyword":["Critical making","Research through design","crafting","making","samplers"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-88742C4FBB4858E49A6C11AA3B10154D"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3658406","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"university of colorado boulder","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Colorado Boulder","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ca","key":"queen s university kingston","loc":["Canada","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Queen's University Kingston","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"at","key":"university of art and industrial design linz","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Art and Industrial Design Linz","used":1},{"affno":"5","country":"us","key":"university of southern california","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"University of Southern California","used":1},{"affno":"6","country":"at","key":"university of salzburg","loc":["Austria","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Salzburg","used":1},{"affno":"7","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Kristina","key":"andersenpau","last":"Andersen","name":"Andersen, Kristina","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Bruna","key":"goveiadarochapau","last":"Goveia Da Rocha","name":"Goveia Da Rocha, Bruna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Laura","key":"devendorfpau","last":"Devendorf","name":"Devendorf, Laura","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Elvia","key":"vasconcelospau","last":"Vasconcelos","name":"Vasconcelos, Elvia","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lee","key":"jonespau","last":"Jones","name":"Jones, Lee","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"4","corresponding":null,"first":"Irene","key":"poschpau","last":"Posch","name":"Posch, Irene","rank":6,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Anuradha Venugopal","key":"reddypau","last":"Reddy","name":"Reddy, Anuradha Venugopal","rank":7,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"5","corresponding":null,"first":"Aisling","key":"kelliherpau","last":"Kelliher","name":"Kelliher, Aisling","rank":8,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"6","corresponding":null,"first":"Verena","key":"fuchsbergerpau","last":"Fuchsberger","name":"Fuchsberger, Verena","rank":9,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"7","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Lone","key":"koefoedhansenpau","last":"Koefoed Hansen","locid":"ae5c1697-dc84-4a67-8ba9-b7cb62bbaea3","name":"Hansen, Lone Koefoed","name_org":"Koefoed Hansen, Lone","orcid":"0000-0002-9877-6362","rank":10,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Etta","key":"sandrypau","last":"Sandry","name":"Sandry, Etta","rank":11,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapedh","last":"Vallgårda","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","rank":12,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jönssonpedh","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Li","rank":13,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":14,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah","key":"fdilialaouipedh","last":"Fdili Alaoui","name":"Fdili Alaoui, Sarah","rank":15,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Cristopher","key":"aledantecpedh","last":"A. Le Dantec","name":"A. Le Dantec, Cristopher","rank":16,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3658406","eisbn":["9798400706325"],"pages":"441-444","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","subtitle":"Companion Publication of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","title":"DIS '24 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198901014"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-146f9ce8-8389-4bf3-9223-3d4dead9340e"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Memoirs for the Future, Imaginations of the Past : Crafting Samplers for Intent and Commitment","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752628","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Artifcial Intelligence (AI) repeatedly match or outperform radiologists in lab experiments. However, real-world implementations of radiological AI-based systems are found to provide little to no clinical value. This paper explores how to design AI for clinical usefulness in diferent contexts. We conducted 19 design sessions and design interventions with 13 radiologists from 7 clinical sites in Denmark and Kenya, based on three iterations of a functional AI-based prototype. Ten sociotechnical dependencies were identifed as crucial for the design of AI in radiology. We conceptualised four technical dimensions that must be confgured to the intended clinical context of use: AI functionality, AI medical focus, AI decision threshold, and AI Explainability. We present four design recommendations on how to address dependencies pertaining to the medical knowledge, clinic type, user expertise level, patient context, and user situation that condition the confguration of these technical dimensions.","author_count":14,"contributors":["Zajac, Hubert Dariusz","Ribeiro, Jorge M.N.","Ingala, Silvia","Gentile, Simona","Wanjohi, Ruth","Gitau, Samuel N.","Carlsen, Jonathan Frederik","Nielsen, Michael Bachmann","Andersen, Tariq Osman"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-811337"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"11-50 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Africa"],"country":["Kenya"],"glorg":["Aga Khan University","All Global Affiliations","The Nairobi Hospital"],"keyword":["Human Centred AI","Machine learning","Performance optimisation","Transferability","Usability","User centred design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-HO","DI-U"],"level3":{"HO":["DI-HO-ALL","DI-HO-CAP"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-HO-CAP","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"it depends configuring ai to improve clinical usefulness across contexts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660707","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-811337","identifier":[{"id":"85200350427","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-e70f5a4a-5d9b-4e73-bda9-a7eb08d4c7da"],"keyword":["AI Interaction","Human-Centred AI","Machine Learning","Performance Optimisation","Transferability","Usability","User-Centred Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-54CC136E45099F2BBEDD3D3F0F3698C1"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660707","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-ND","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444201270/It_depends.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"capital region of denmark","l2":"DI-HO","l2n":"Hospitals","l3":"DI-HO-CAP","l3nl":"Capital Region of Denmark","l3nn":"Capital Region of Denmark","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Capital Region of Denmark","namevar":["Copenhagen University Hospital - Rigshospitalet"],"nora_code":"DI-HO-CAP","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"ke","key":"the nairobi hospital","loc":["Kenya","Africa"],"name":"The Nairobi Hospital","used":1},{"affno":"4","country":"ke","key":"aga khan university","loc":["Kenya","Africa"]