{"abstract":"In this paper we introduce the experimental prototype MoSS (Modular Smart Speaker). MoSS is a modular speech synthesis smart speaker system, and a feature-rich and capable platform that resembles and functions as an intelligent smart speaker, while featuring extended functions for advanced audio processing. MoSS is composed byanumberofsoftwareandhardwarecomponents, allowing people to customize, modify and modulate its synthetic voice in real-time. Through playfully combining the different tools and parameters, MoSS facilitates an investigation of human/machine interaction with voice controlled smart home objects, with a focus on the exploration of sound and voice synthesis. We present the process leading the creation of MoSS, how it works and the preliminary results from using the device to inspire novel vocal imaginaries in synthetic voice design.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Lyngsø Knudsen, Søren","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S02-086.98-822873"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Smart Speakers"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"moss unfolding playful imaginaries of synthetic voice design through a modular smart speaker","src":["itu","ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665428","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-086.98-822873","identifier":[{"id":"85198906620","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-69e87e34-8f72-4699-b684-22c0dcaa5a29","ku-95bd98f4-19df-496b-9dca-e0634e6476b4"],"keyword":["Exploratory Prototyping","Modular Synthesizers","Smart Speakers","Synthetic Voice Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-AD14EE220BCF9D0CFD39227B75F7F781"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665428","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/108403558/MoSSDIS2024Compantion.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Arts and Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"lyngsøknudsenpau","last":"Lyngsø Knudsen","name":"Lyngsø Knudsen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Søren Lyngsø","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren Lyngsø","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","orcid":"0000-0001-6275-8966","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3665428","pages":"342-346","status":"p","title":"Companion Publication of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference (DIS '24 Companion)"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198906620"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-69e87e34-8f72-4699-b684-22c0dcaa5a29","ku-95bd98f4-19df-496b-9dca-e0634e6476b4"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen","KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"MoSS: Unfolding Playful Imaginaries of Synthetic Voice Design through a Modular Smart Speaker","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-086.98-822873","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Long COVID is a new illness, and we still lack medical knowledge about possible treatments. This has led to the independent adoption of fitness tracking technologies for the management of long COVID. Through semi-structured interviews with 21 people with long COVID who used fitness tracking technologies, we found that fitness tracking devices were used to pace energy through finding correlations between activities and data, provide proof of illness to themselves, healthcare providers and friends and family, and to help gain a sense of agency and control during a new and enigmatic illness. Our findings support and extend design openings for the development of “pacing technologies”. These include the importance of customization and supporting the user in their recovery if appropriate, applying strategies for mitigating anxiety when tracking, facilitating the sharing of pacing data with friends and family and healthcare providers, and supporting users in identifying the optimal components of rest.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Homewood, Sarah","Just, Kari Okholm","Johansson, Olivia Bramm"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-760561"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Chronic fatigue","Chronic illness","Misuse","Pacing","Self tracking","Sensemaking","Use","long COVID","pacing technologies","post COVID syndrome"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the unanticipated use of fitness tracking technologies during post covid syndrome","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402489864/The_Unanticipated_Use_of_Fitness_Tracking.pdf","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-760561","identifier":[{"id":"85200359477","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-f6899244-d2af-4cba-b1be-e8b04d003c45"],"keyword":["chronic fatigue","chronic illness","fitness tracking","long COVID","misuse","pacing","pacing technologies","post-COVID syndrome","self-tracking","sensemaking","use"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-B08F16932140A3A946198FAE49EDEB7A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/402489864/The_Unanticipated_Use_of_Fitness_Tracking.pdf","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centred Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Sarah","key":"homewoodpau","last":"Homewood","locid":"e6edf1cc-cfc0-4304-8638-989154e536d8","name":"Homewood, Sarah","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Kari Okholm","key":"justpau","last":"Just","name":"Just, Kari Okholm","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Olivia Bramm","key":"johanssonpau","last":"Johansson","name":"Johansson, Olivia Bramm","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661617","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"556-570","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","series":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200359477"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-f6899244-d2af-4cba-b1be-e8b04d003c45"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Unanticipated Use of Fitness Tracking Technologies During Post-COVID Syndrome","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-760561","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"author_count":4,"contributors":["Knudsen, Søren Lyngsø","Fritsch, Jonas","Jørgensen, Stina Marie Hasse","Ada, Ada Ada"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-829518"],"filters":{"added":"2025-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the climate change smart speakers probing novel vocal imaginaries","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3677045.3685480","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-829518","identifier":[{"id":"85206569862","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-a017156b-21a4-48ab-a7d2-cc5a26905049"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-488095C33BC5B9EFB22A2A5597659CCF"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Humanities, Department of Arts and Cultural Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","first":"Søren Lyngsø","key":"knudsenpau","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Søren Lyngsø","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Stina Marie Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","locid":"b5e7e7eb-531c-4657-b416-4b81fe475ada","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Marie Hasse","orcid":"0000-0001-6275-8966","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Ada Ada","key":"adapau","last":"Ada","name":"Ada, Ada Ada","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685480","status":"p","title":"The Climate Change Smart Speakers: Probing Novel Vocal Imaginaries"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206569862"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-a017156b-21a4-48ab-a7d2-cc5a26905049"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Climate Change Smart Speakers: Probing Novel Vocal Imaginaries","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-829518","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"In this pictorial, we present the process leading to the creation of N/ERWER, an affectively engaging interactive prototype exploring personal domestic grief practices. N/ERV/ER symbolises a physical presence of the Intangible affective experiences associated with grief as an ongoing connection to the deceased in the present. N/ERV/ER was developed in a Research through Design process fueled by both personal accounts and participatory engagements using various design probes exploring experiences of loss following the death of a loved one. In this pictorial, we unfold the theoretical, methodological, and material dimensions of this process to show how designers can accommodate grief in design practice as a way of utilising and materialising the affective forces present in such sensitive contexts.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Ravn, Nicklas Engelbrecht","Sveegaard, Nadja Striib","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-759392"],"filters":{"added":"2024-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Form giving","Grief","Probes","Research through Design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"materialising affective experiences designing for personal grief practices","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660753","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-759392","identifier":[{"id":"85200336159","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-31349ac6-5fe1-4699-bc3f-857fdcbe21a7"],"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Form-giving","Grief","Probes","Research through Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-E26E3C447514774F0AFA0C51CC51C925"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC-SA","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660753","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Digitalization, Democracy, and Governance, Welfare Technology - Policy - People - Practices"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicklas Engelbrecht","key":"ravnpau","last":"Ravn","locid":"20685b27-43b0-4170-bcf8-3cc28832d2e7","name":"Ravn, Nicklas Engelbrecht","orcid":"0009-0001-6144-0451","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Nadja Striib","key":"sveegaardpau","last":"Sveegaard","name":"Sveegaard, Nadja Striib","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3660753","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"685-698","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200336159"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-31349ac6-5fe1-4699-bc3f-857fdcbe21a7"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Materialising affective experiences : Designing for personal grief practices","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-759392","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"This critique presents and discusses the research contributing to and following the creation and exhibition of the interactive Extended Reality (XR) installation called UDREDNING (English: Diagnosing), which aims to convey the experience of being a parent to a child undergoing socio-medical diagnosis for a rare disease. Being a parent in such a situation often entails great affective and emotional uncertainty, heavy logistics and numerous encounters with people and (digital) systems within social welfare services, public healthcare and bureaucracies. Since these children are pre-diagnosis, they rarely fit neatly into the existing systems, which they must engage with. Due to the open-ended nature of such processes, parents often find themselves alone and marginalized, in lack of an overview, and unsure where to get the help they need. Based on diaries, social media entries and interviews with parents to children during or recently after their experiences of a diagnosing process, an artist created UDREDNING in collaboration with the two authors. The installation uses digital sound, video and a tablet that extends the reality of these parents so people can relate to their experiences of the uncertainties and systemic entanglements characterizing their situation. In this article, we explore the different forms of critique opened by the research and exhibition of the project through concepts across STS, HCI, design and art. We argue that UDREDNING creates an embodied and experiential space of critical resonance extending lived experience into a digital re-activation in an affectively engaging interactive setup.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776459"],"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Extended reality","Human Computer Interaction","Parental experiences","Science and Technology Studies"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"udredning an extended reality artwork for affectively engaging with diagnosing processes","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85206575123","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776459","identifier":[{"id":"85206575123","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-f4a4b58a-122e-4db0-8731-62f4e040626b"],"keyword":["Extended Reality","Human-Computer Interaction","Interactive art installation","Parental experiences","Science and Technology Studies"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-0D6AC73DBD7441F6D554653A8CFFC4B5"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3677045.3685491","pages":"1-9","status":"p","subtitle":"Adjunct Proceedings of the 2024 Nordic Conference on Human-Computer Interaction","title":"NordiCHI '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85206575123"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-f4a4b58a-122e-4db0-8731-62f4e040626b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"UDREDNING: : an Extended Reality Artwork for Affectively Engaging with Diagnosing Processes","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776459","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The mental and emotional burden of living with a chronic disease, such as Rheumatoid Arthritis (RA), calls for a better understanding of how we can support people in coping through affectively designed healthcare technologies. This paper presents findings from an ongoing research project concerned with redesigning an existing self-tracking app towards better supporting affective dimensions of living with RA. On the basis of an exploratory, intervention-based design study, we present three overall affective needs feeding into three design opportunities for cultivating affective and emotional dimensions in the redesign of the app; 1) creating a digital room for emotional response, 2) offering a space for mindfulness and 3) helping people to own their RA story. Our results emphasize the need for HCI and design researchers to approach the design of healthcare technology holistically, which includes exploring affective interactions that empower people to develop more sustainable coping strategies.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Kühn, Lena","Boer, Laurens","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-798563"],"filters":{"added":"2025-04","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Health","Mental wellbeing","Rheumatoid arthritis"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"exploring app based affective interactions for people with rheumatoid arthritis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.895","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-798563","ids":["itu-ded5b5ed-01c7-4c36-a207-212a1efc1f7b"],"keyword":["affective interaction design","affective interactions","health","mental wellbeing","rheumatoid arthritis"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-55B7F02765B6352A391DBACCA8CCE820"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY-NC","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.21606/drs.2024.895","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"kühnpau","last":"Kühn","name":"Kühn, Lena","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Laurens","key":"boerpau","last":"Boer","locid":"25a5a0d6-404b-419c-9502-b246525617a2","name":"Boer, Laurens","orcid":"0000-0001-9723-5516","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.21606/drs.2024.895","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of DRS2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ded5b5ed-01c7-4c36-a207-212a1efc1f7b"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Exploring app-based affective interactions for people with rheumatoid arthritis","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-798563","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Image-generation AI models have triggered a paradigm shift in how we can express ourselves in visual art. Despite their widespread use in a short amount of time, embedding these models into interactive artifacts is still largely unexplored. In this pictorial, we unpack the design and development process of GenFrame, an image generating picture frame that utilizes generative AI capabilities to mimic traditional paintings. Our work details the necessary steps to integrate generative AI into interactive artifacts and highlights important design considerations for controlling image-generation models in order to achieve specific design intents. Our insights provide interaction designers with a more comprehensive understanding and approach towards utilizing image-generation AI models for interactive artifacts. A demo can be viewed at https://youtu.be/1rhW4fazaBY.","author_count":9,"contributors":["Kun, Peter","Freiberger, Matthias","Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","Risi, Sebastian"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-809172"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Cultural heritage","Interaction design","Museums"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU","DI-U-KU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"genframe embedding generative ai into interactive artifacts","src":["ku"],"src-code":["DI-U-KU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-809172","identifier":[{"id":"85198907112","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"keyword":["cultural heritage","image-generation AI models","interaction design","museums"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-A6705AE38DF230903B57FF9F32135C96"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://curis.ku.dk/ws/files/444850486/GenFrame_Embedding_Generative_AI_Into_Interactive_Artifacts.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3660750","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"ku university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-KU","l3nl":"University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"KU University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"KU University of Copenhagen","namevar":["Københavns Universitet, Faculty of Science, Department of Computer Science, Pioneer AI (P1AI)"],"nora_code":"DI-U-KU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","first":"Peter","key":"kunpau","last":"Kun","name":"Kun, Peter","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","first":"Matthias Anton","key":"freibergerpau","last":"Freiberger","locid":"58e199e0-71a9-4f89-a2b1-97346c7d29e8","name":"Freiberger, Matthias","name_org":"Freiberger, Matthias Anton","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Anders Sundnes","key":"løvliepau","last":"Løvlie","name":"Løvlie, Anders Sundnes","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","first":"Sebastian","key":"risipau","last":"Risi","name":"Risi, Sebastian","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":9,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3660750","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"714-727","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198907112"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities","University of Copenhagen"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["ku-18e3512e-ba5e-4ca6-8adf-ac655a93298b"],"src":["KU University of Copenhagen"],"title":"GenFrame – Embedding Generative AI Into Interactive Artifacts","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-809172","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"The recent leaps in complexity and fluency of Large Language Models (LLMs) mean that, for the first time in human history, people can interact with computers using natural language alone. This creates monumental possibilities of automation and accessibility of computing, but also raises severe security and safety threats: When everyone can interact with LLMs, everyone can potentially break into the systems running LLMs. All it takes is creative use of language. This paper presents Hacc-Man, a game which challenges its players to \"jailbreak\"an LLM: subvert the LLM to output something that it is not intended to. Jailbreaking is at the intersection between creative problem solving and LLM security. The purpose of the game is threefold: 1. To heighten awareness of the risks of deploying fragile LLMs in everyday systems, 2. To heighten people's self-efficacy in interacting with LLMs, and 3. To discover the creative problem solving strategies, people deploy in this novel context.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Valentim, Matheus","Falk, Jeanette","Inie, Nanna"],"cuid":["S02-083.60-767050"],"event":{"end":"2024-06-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-06-01","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2025-01","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Creative problem solving","Creativity","Hacking","LLM Security","arcade games","jailbreaking","red teaming"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"hacc man an arcade game for jailbreaking llms","src":["aau","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665432","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-083.60-767050","identifier":[{"id":"85198900811","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-d4e09114-48ca-48e7-a99e-5487589adead","itu-edfb6f9b-47d4-4cb7-90ca-81c2d2e5350d"],"keyword":["LLM security","arcade games.","creative problem solving","creativity","creativity, creative problem solving","hacking","jailbreaking","red teaming"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-1C50D525E2B9187CABF608774AE6814C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY 4.0","type":"loc","url":"https://vbn.aau.dk/ws/files/753240355/3656156.3665432.pdf","version":"Published Version"},{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3656156.3665432","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Computing Education Research","IT University of Copenhagen, Computer Science","IT University of Copenhagen, Data Science, Machine Learning"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"","corresponding":null,"first":"Matheus","key":"valentimpau","last":"Valentim","name":"Valentim, Matheus","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jeanette","key":"falkpau","last":"Falk","locid":"5084b27d-c3fe-43a4-9fe3-3ecd28908952","name":"Falk, Jeanette","orcid":"0000-0001-7278-9344","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Nanna","key":"iniepau","last":"Inie","locid":"e23e8096-59cb-4ef6-af48-ce9d806fd1eb","name":"Inie, Nanna","orcid":"0000-0002-5375-9542","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapedh","last":"Vallgårda","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jönssonpedh","last":"Jönsson","name":"Jönsson, Li","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3656156.3665432","eisbn":["9798400706325"],"pages":"338-341","place":"New York, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery (ACM)","status":"p","title":"DIS 2024 - Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85198900811"],"search":{"DAF":["Aalborg University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["aau-d4e09114-48ca-48e7-a99e-5487589adead","itu-edfb6f9b-47d4-4cb7-90ca-81c2d2e5350d"],"src":["AAU Aalborg University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Hacc-Man : An Arcade Game for Jailbreaking LLMs","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-083.60-767050","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
{"abstract":"Collaboration in distributed mixed reality (MR) creates co-presence illusions by bringing a digital representation of the remote collaborator into the local user’s physical space. However, constraints in each physical environment, such as diferent spatial layouts and furniture, can hinder collaboration and momentarily break the illusion of co-location. Since the remote user’s physical space is invisible to the local user, the source of the interaction problem is often imperceptible, leading to familiar real-world interactions suddenly feeling unfamiliar—a concept we term the Jamais Vu Efect. In this paper, we conceptualise and demonstrate this efect through a fve-part user study that elicits the user experience of the Jamais Vu Efect in MR. We contribute a shared vocabulary and understanding of spatial interface design challenges to help designers and researchers discuss and improve distributed collaboration in MR.","author_count":8,"contributors":["Wong, Emily","Grønbæk, Jens Emil","Velloso, Eduardo"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-752693"],"event":{"end":"2024-07-05","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2024-07-01","title":"2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference, DIS 2024","year":"2024"},"filters":{"added":"2024-09","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["OECD","Oceania"],"country":["Australia"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Melbourne","University of Sydney"],"keyword":["Co presence","Distributed Collaboration","Mixed reality"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"the jamais vu efect understanding the fragile illusion of co presence in mixed reality","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661574","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-752693","identifier":[{"id":"85200390499","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-277059a1-9b90-44e6-8dc8-c0a583fff096"],"keyword":["Jamais Vu Efect","co-presence","distributed collaboration","mixed reality"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-1A3A064A30CB02F6ECA3EE0CD6889418"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","license":"CC BY","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1145/3643834.3661574","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"au","key":"university of melbourne","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Melbourne","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Natural Sciences, Department of Computer Science"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"au","key":"university of sydney","loc":["Australia","Oceania","OECD"],"name":"University of Sydney","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Emily","key":"wongpau","last":"Wong","name":"Wong, Emily","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Jens Emil","key":"grønbækpau","last":"Grønbæk","locid":"cb34ed1e-a18d-4b6d-8f80-1cace0ea64c2","name":"Grønbæk, Jens Emil","orcid":"0000-0002-9566-7195","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Eduardo","key":"vellosopau","last":"Velloso","name":"Velloso, Eduardo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Anna","key":"vallgardapedh","last":"Vallgarda","name":"Vallgarda, Anna","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Li","key":"jonssonpedh","last":"Jonsson","name":"Jonsson, Li","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":6,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Sarah Fdili","key":"alaouipedh","last":"Alaoui","name":"Alaoui, Sarah Fdili","rank":7,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Christopher A.","key":"ledantecpedh","last":"Le Dantec","name":"Le Dantec, Christopher A.","rank":8,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3643834.3661574","eisbn":["9798400705830"],"pages":"2227-2246","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery, Inc.","status":"p","subtitle":"Proceedings of the 2024 ACM Designing Interactive Systems Conference","title":"DIS '24"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85200390499"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-277059a1-9b90-44e6-8dc8-c0a583fff096"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"The Jamais Vu Efect : Understanding the Fragile Illusion of Co-presence in Mixed Reality","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-752693","year":"2024","yearsub":"2024"}
