esign, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Interaction Design Research Group","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Joanna","key":"saadsulonenpau","last":"Saad-Sulonen","name":"Saad-Sulonen, Joanna","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Giacomo","key":"poderipau","last":"Poderi","name":"Poderi, Giacomo","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3546155.3547287","eisbn":["9781450396998"],"pages":"1-9","place":"New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","series":"Proceedings of NordiCHI","status":"p","title":"NordiCHI '22: Nordic Human-Computer Interaction Conference"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85140901735"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-49280f14-5171-4331-ad6c-6003ae4b9f6a"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"The Problem(s) of Caring for the Commons","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382359","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"Keywords: Socio-medical diagnosis, research through design and art, encountering the state, This talk is a report from an ongoing research trough art/design project on giving expression to experiences of parents to children undergoing socio-medical diagnosis (udredning) including experiences of encountering ‘the state’ in this situation. The project’s current aim is transforming interviews with such parents into an interactive audio-visual art installation intended to provoke reflections and a broader conversation on the matter. Today, Danish citizens has arguably become increasingly responsible for managing their various affairs in relation to the state. This is due to many causes, including digitalization. Such responsibilities arguably intensify in already emotionally challenging situations, such as e.g. undergoing divorce or being unemployed. Parents to children undergoing diagnosis express that they feel like becoming ‘project managers’ or ‘caseworkers’ for their children’s affairs and the lives of their families. The institutions with which they must engage quickly multiply and the state seems to be experienced as unexpectedly complex - more like a ’semiotic haze’ (Fabian Muniesa) rather than like a coordinated ‘whole’. Among other things, such parents become the main choreographers of an increasingly complex story of their child, which is important not only in their various encounters with institutions and for the trajectory of diagnosis and living with such, but also in managing relations to their families, neighbours, and friends. This talk will present how this research and art/design project developed from initial ideas to the resulting art-installation, which it is the plan to make public in the fall of 2022.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Gad, Christopher","Fritsch, Jonas","Jacobsen, Mogens"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383610"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Interactive audio visual art","Parent experiences","Research through Design","Socio medical diagnosis","State encounters"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"expressing undergoing diagnosis","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dca","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-383610","ids":["itu-a0c1cec3-631b-4fc3-9d53-d562c8dfe0f6"],"keyword":["Interactive audio-visual art","Parent experiences","Research through design","Socio-medical diagnosis","State encounters"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-7588C96A7709CD64798E33CE29A04302"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Center for Information Security and Trust","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Christopher","key":"gadpau","last":"Gad","locid":"d55dab65-fffe-4da4-a383-cfcf5ee3a8cd","name":"Gad, Christopher","orcid":"0000-0002-1631-5483","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Mogens","key":"jacobsenpau","last":"Jacobsen","name":"Jacobsen, Mogens","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"No Review","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-a0c1cec3-631b-4fc3-9d53-d562c8dfe0f6"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Expressing undergoing Diagnosis","type":"Conference Abstract","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383610","year":"2022","yearsub":"2022"}
{"abstract":"'Soundscapes' are an increasingly active topic in Human-Computer Interaction (HCI) and interaction design. From mapping acoustic environments through sound recordings to designing compositions as interventions, soundscapes appear as a recurring theme across a wide body of HCI research. Based on this growing interest, now is the time to explore the types of studies in which soundscapes provide a valuable lens to HCI research. In this paper, we review papers from conferences sponsored or co-sponsored by the ACM Special Interest Group on Computer-Human Interaction in which the term 'soundscape' occurs. We analyse a total of 235 papers to understand the role of soundscapes as a research focus and identify untapped opportunities for soundscape research within HCI. We identify two common soundscape conceptualisations: (1) Acoustic environments and (2) Compositions, and describe what characterises studies into each concept and the hybrid forms that also occur. On the basis of this, we carve out a foundation for future soundscape research in HCI as a methodological anchor to form a common ground and support this growing research interest. Finally, we offer five recommendations for further research into soundscapes within HCI.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Johansen, Stine Schmieg","van Berkel, Niels","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-120964"],"event":{"end":"2022-06-17","start":"2022-06-13","title":"17th ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems, DIS 2022","year":"2022"},"filters":{"added":"2022-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Audio","HCI","Literature review","SOUNDS","Soundscape","Theory"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AAU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"characterising soundscape research in human computer interaction","src":["aau"],"src-code":["DI-U-AAU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.scopus.com/inward/record.url?scp=85133568677&partnerID=8YFLogxK","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-120964","identifier":[{"id":"85133568677","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["aau-f3e4abd1-7791-448e-8736-84f50b25917d"],"keyword":["HCI","Literature Review","Soundscape","audio","sounds","theory"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AC818B105EF7D8B5D98705BD133AD348"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"aau aalborg university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AAU","l3nl":"Aalborg University","l3nn":"AAU Aalborg University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AAU Aalborg University","namevar":["Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Architecture, Design and Media Technology, Human Machine Interaction","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science","Aalborg University, The Technical Faculty of IT and Design, Department of Computer Science, Human-Centered Computing"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AAU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Stine Schmieg","key":"johansenpau","last":"Johansen","locid":"04546f61-a1e4-4f11-90db-a305c42e53b4","name":"Johansen, Stine Schmieg","orcid":"0000-0002-8451-5444","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Niels","key":"vanberkelpau","last":"van Berkel","locid":"4088b4e4-37