{"abstract":"In focusing on interfacial productions of modulations rather than semiotic constructions of meaning or content, the perspective is set on exploring affects in relation to events. Or rather, the felt intensities of interfacial folding-unfolding modulations enable us to experience new potentials and qualities—or as phrased by Brian Massumi—becoming aware of “the thinking-feeling of what really happens” (Massumi 2011, 67). Massumi explores the immediate prehensions as potentials for change (or events) in whatever happens. In my presentation of three artworks I use the term ‘modulation’ to explore whether the signaletic material and the folding capacity of interfaces might give access to qualitative differentials or potentials.","author_count":4,"contributors":["Thomsen, Bodil Marie Stavning"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-167354"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Affect","Brian Massumi","Deleuze","Diagram","EVENTS","Folding","Interfaces","Jesper Just","Modulation","receptacle","signaletic material"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"interfacial modulation of affect on the creation of events in contemporary artworks","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22387/IMBAIE.07","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-167354","ids":["au-42c22758-c6af-48ea-bebb-e49e4116f9fd"],"keyword":["Anna Munster","Brian Massumi","Deleuze","Erin Manning","Jacob Kirkegaard","Jesper Just","Joshua Portway","Katinka Fogh","Lise Autogena","affect","diagram","events","folding","interfaces","modulation","receptacle","signaletic material","thinking-feeling"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-2-8D0B55F0EFC5E49D119093F3DD381435"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.22387/IMBAIE.07","version":"Published Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Scandinavian Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Bodil Marie Stavning","key":"thomsenpau","last":"Thomsen","locid":"055e1b94-febb-4a3e-acd7-a200699c386c","name":"Thomsen, Bodil Marie Stavning","orcid":"0000-0003-0568-0386","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Thomsen","key":"bodilmariestavningpedh","last":"Bodil Marie Stavning","name":"Bodil Marie Stavning, Thomsen","rank":2,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jette","key":"kofoedpedh","last":"Kofoed","name":"Kofoed, Jette","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpedh","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.22387/imbaie.07","isbn":["9798729524525"],"pages":"165-185","place":"Vancouver","publisher":"Imbricate! Press","status":"p","title":"Affects, Interfaces, Events"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-42c22758-c6af-48ea-bebb-e49e4116f9fd"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Interfacial Modulation of Affect : On the Creation of Events in Contemporary Artworks","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-167354","year":"2021","yearsub":"2021"}
{"abstract":"This paper reports on our ongoing research focusing on cultivating and exploring the topic of what we refer to as breathing commons. We approach breathing as an affective and somatic bodily function that ties the individual with the collective, and through that aim to foster affective commoning among bodies. We present two workshops, one physical and one online, that we have ran amongst our research group on breathing commons. Three themes emerged from the analysis of the workshop activities: a) The body as a membrane, b) feelings of intimacy, vulnerability and awkwardness, and c) mutual engagement and care. These show a path towards engaging with breathing, and potentially with other bodily functions and biodata, aiming to open up the design space of doing affective commoning through bodily functions that act as a connection between bodies – both human and non-human.","author_count":7,"contributors":["Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","Kühn, Lena","Ryding, Karin","Hartmann, Mai","Fritsch, Jonas","Foverskov, Maria"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382594"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"country":["Sweden"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Malmö University"],"keyword":["Affective Commoning","Breathing Commons","Collective Intimacy","Design Space Biodata","Somatic Bodily Function"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"breathing commons affective and somatic relations between self and others","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86283295/BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382594","ids":["itu-595a8ea9-4a43-4e61-8281-413de86655f4"],"keyword":["Affective Commoning","Breathing Commons","Collective Intimacy","Design Space Biodata","Somatic Bodily Function"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-53B577E599AB9DC688F3018C6D5B5D8C"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/86283295/BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS_.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Vasiliki-Tsaknaki/publication/353945970_BREATHING_COMMONS_AFFECTIVE_AND_SOMATIC_RELATIONS_BETWEEN_SELF_AND_OTHERS/links/611b70df1e95fe241ad87458/BREATHING-COMMONS-AFFECTIVE-AND-SOMATIC-RELATIONS-BETWEEN-SELF-AND-OTHERS.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"se","key":"malmö university","loc":["Sweden","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Malmö University","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Vasiliki","key":"tsaknakipau","last":"Tsaknaki","locid":"805cae2a-3462-4130-88de-cc7d94aec0a5","name":"Tsaknaki, Vasiliki","orcid":"0000-0003-2235-6078","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Stina Hasse","key":"jørgensenpau","last":"Jørgensen","name":"Jørgensen, Stina Hasse","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Lena","key":"kühnpau","last":"Kühn","name":"Kühn, Lena","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":