Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381780","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"We are living in a time of ecological and humanitarian crisis that requires imminent action from the joint fields of HCI and interaction design. In a very palpable way, we seem to be moving towards the “end of the world” (certainly, as we have known it). This workshop addresses three concrete end-of-world challenges – the end of nature, end of culture and end of the human – to contribute to a much-needed design research agenda and to build community in the process. The workshop will explore how the design of technology can support a fairer and more secure set of futures by considering these three end-states and what we, as participants (both contributing to futures and living with the outcomes), can offer to improve the options. Contributions to theory and practice will be welcome.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Loi, Daria","Light, Ann"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383796"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["America, North","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom","United States"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Intel","University of Sussex"],"keyword":["Ecological Crisis","Futures thinking","Human Computer Interaction HCI","Humanitarian Crisis","Interaction design"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing at the end of the world","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84846229/DIS19_Workshop_End_of_World_FINAL_Submission.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S01-000.00-383796","identifier":[{"id":"85069513328","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-ae2ea32f-e0f1-49d3-964f-bd8b79197b22"],"keyword":["Ecological Crisis","Futures Thinking","Human-Computer Interaction (HCI)","Humanitarian Crisis","Interaction Design"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-CE6FE4E01C5765437E2F1B6B765D61AB"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84846229/DIS19_Workshop_End_of_World_FINAL_Submission.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"us","key":"intel","loc":["United States","America, North","OECD"],"name":"Intel","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"gb","key":"university of sussex","loc":["United Kingdom","Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"name":"University of Sussex","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Daria","key":"loipau","last":"Loi","name":"Loi, Daria","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Ann","key":"lightpau","last":"Light","name":"Light, Ann","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3301019.3319999","pages":"369-372","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"Publication of the 2019 Designing Interactive Systems Conference 2019","title":"DIS'19 Companion"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85069513328"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-ae2ea32f-e0f1-49d3-964f-bd8b79197b22"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Designing at the End of the World","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383796","year":"2019","yearsub":"2019"}
{"abstract":"In this paper, we develop the notion of design archives to understand how different forms of knowledge are systematically accumulated and shared in and across design processes. Drawing on philosophy and media theory, we present a working definition of design archives as more than documentation. Through an interview study, we investigate how various archives systematically inform design work and govern the way design processes are represented and reflected upon. The study provides insights into an abundance of tools used to access, record, store and share information. We highlight the difference between personal, shared, and public archives, different archival barriers for sharing, how prototypes act as (an)archival conduits of design potentials, and how information (and people) tend to get lost in the archives. Finally, we discuss how a design archival approach might help identify power relations in design while also facilitating a move from 'dead' to 'living' archives in design work.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Rasmussen, Søren","Fritsch, Jonas","Hansen, Nicolai Brodersen"],"cuid":["S02-089.89-704188"],"event":{"acronym":"OzCHI","end":"2019-12-05","place":"Perth/Fremantle, au","start":"2019-12-02","title":"31st Australian Conference on Human-Computer-Interaction, OzCHI 2019","year":"2019"},"filters":{"added":"2021-10","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"continent":["Europe, EU","OECD"],"country":["Netherlands"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","Eindhoven University of Technology"],"keyword":["Archival Barriers","Design Archives","Design knowledge","Design processes","Design research","Design theory","Documentation","Knowledge Accumulation","Prototypes as Archives"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum","sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"a design archival approach to knowledge production in design research and practice","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84846269/A_Design_Archival_Approach_to_Knowledge_Production_in_Design_Research_and_Practice_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"},"id":"S02-089.89-704188","identifier":[{"id":"85078695694","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-7b250652-c6cc-4143-b79e-6666ae7a8f4d","itu-f2ad70c4-0896-4858-bc1b-7c3e913ce22b"],"keyword":["Archival Barriers","Design archives","Design knowledge","Design processes","Design research","Design theory","Digital support tools","Documentation","Knowledge Accumulation","Prototypes as Archives"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities","Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-983A72C994D814CEEB5C03A8FC3EE841"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/84846269/A_Design_Archival_Approach_to_Knowledge_Production_in_Design_Research_and_Practice_2_.pdf","version":"Pre-print"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Department of Digital Design and Information Studies"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Human-Computer Interaction and Design, Affective Interactions & Relations Lab","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"nl","key":"eindhoven university of technology","loc":["Netherlands","Europe, EU","OECD"],"name":"Eindhoven University of Technology","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Søren","key":"rasmussenpau","last":"Rasmussen","locid":"190063a9-b536-4c8a-8721-10f5cfa41b7b","name":"Rasmussen, Søren","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Nicolai Brodersen","key":"hansenpau","last":"Hansen","name":"Hansen, Nicolai Brodersen","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/3369457.3369476","eisbn":["9781450376969"],"pages":"233-243","place":"New York","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 31st Australian Conference on Human-Computer-Interaction, OzCHI 2019"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85078695694"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-7b250652-c6cc-4143-b79e-6666ae7a8f4d","itu-f2ad70c4-0896-4858-bc1b-7c3e913ce22b"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"A Design Archival Approach to Knowledge Production in Design Research and Practice","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-089.89-704188","year":"2019","yearsub":2020}
