{"abstract":"This paper presents a theoretical framework for analyzing the aesthetics of participation of media architecture. The framework is based on a close reading of French philosopher Jacques Rancière and provides four points of emphasis: modes of sense perception, forms of engagement, community and emancipation. The framework is put to use in the analysis of three experimental media architectural projects; Ekkomaten/Echoes from Møllevangen, the coMotion Bench and FeltRadio. We discuss the findings from this analysis and outline future perspectives on how to develop and use the framework prospectively in the design of media architectural projects and other interactive environments.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Grönvall, Erik","Breinbjerg, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-776420"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics of participation","Interactive Environments","Jacques Rancière","Media architecture","Sense Perception"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyzing the aesthetics of participation of media architecture","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82943432/MAB2016_AestheticsOfParticipation_CAMERAREADY.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-776420","identifier":[{"id":"85015397417","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-82ddc544-072e-4264-a30c-f6e82a03f7ea"],"keyword":["Aesthetics of Participation","Interactive Environments","Jacques Rancière","Media Architecture","Sense Perception"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-9B6E766D7FA5239E0EDB4FBD824AAC22"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"loc","url":"https://pure.itu.dk/ws/files/82943432/MAB2016_AestheticsOfParticipation_CAMERAREADY.pdf","version":"Authors Final Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","IT University of Copenhagen, Play, Culture, and AI, Media, Art & Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"2","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"grönvallpau","last":"Grönvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"breinbjergpau","last":"Breinbjerg","name":"Breinbjerg, Morten","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2946803.2946807","eisbn":["ISBN: 9781450347495"],"place":"ACM New York, NY, USA","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","title":"Proceedings of the 3rd Conference on Media Architecture Biennale"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-85015397417"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-82ddc544-072e-4264-a30c-f6e82a03f7ea"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Analyzing the Aesthetics of Participation of Media Architecture","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-776420","year":"2016","yearsub":"2018"}
{"abstract":"The project “Audio Satellites – overhearing everyday life” consists of a number of mobile listening devices (audio satellites) from which sound is distributed in real time to a server and made available for listening and mixing through a web interface. The audio satellites can either be carried around or displaced arbitrarily in a given landscape. In the web interface, the different sound streams from the individual satellites can be mixed together to form a cooperative soundscape. The project thus allows people to tune into and explore the overheard soundscape of everyday life in a collaborative and creative process of active listening.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Breinbjerg, Morten","Højlund, Marie Koldkjær","Riis, Morten S.","Fritsch, Jonas","Kirkegaard, Jonas R."],"cuid":["S01-000.00-381379"],"event":{"acronym":"COOP","end":"2016-05-27","place":"Trento, it","start":"2016-05-22","title":"COOP 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Active listening process","Collaborative soundscape","Mobile listening devices","Real time sound distribution","Web based audio mixing"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-U"],"level3":{"OT":["University College Southern Denmark"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"audio satellites overhearing everyday life","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.springer.com/us/book/9783319334639","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-381379","ids":["itu-0815f3ae-fbcd-4ab8-8635-a53e00b59e4f"],"keyword":["Active listening process","Collaborative soundscape","Mobile listening devices","Real-time sound distribution","Web-based audio mixing"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-4-B15DB158ADA02A588F4092DA670CB258"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"dk","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","country":"dk","key":"miscellaneous","l2":"DI-OT","l2n":"Miscellaneous","l3":"DI-OT","l3nl":"Other Research","l3nn":"Miscellaneous","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Miscellaneous","namevar":["University College Southern Denmark"],"nora_code":"DI-OT","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten","key":"breinbjergpau","last":"Breinbjerg","name":"Breinbjerg, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Marie Koldkjær","key":"højlundpau","last":"Højlund","name":"Højlund, Marie Koldkjær","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Morten S.","key":"riispau","last":"Riis","name":"Riis, Morten S.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas R.","key":"kirkegaardpau","last":"Kirkegaard","name":"Kirkegaard, Jonas R.","rank":5,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-33464-6_18","eisbn":["9783319334646"],"isbn":["9783319334639"],"pages":"297-302","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"COOP 2016: Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on the Design of Cooperative Systems, 23-27 May 2016, Trento, Italy","volume":"Part II"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Miscellaneous","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-OT","DI-OT-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Miscellaneous","Other Research","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-0815f3ae-fbcd-4ab8-8635-a53e00b59e4f"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Audio Satellites – Overhearing Everyday Life","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-381379","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"Radio waves surround us but still they remain largely undetected by our senses. Unless we use specifically tuned hardware, such as FM radios, cell phones or WiFi modems, human beings cannot perceive wirelessly transmitted data. This paper presents FeltRadio, a portable and wireless technology that makes it possible to turn radio signals into visual and tactile stimuli as a form of sensorial augmentation. FeltRadio explores and makes us reflect upon what it would be like if we could sense, and feel, wireless traffic such as WiFi or Bluetooth. We present the technological design behind FeltRadio and the outcome of two exploratory studies with the technology focused on people's experience of being able to suddenly sense and make sense of wireless traffic. We discuss the possible qualities of this embodied experience of FeltRadio and point to future experiments with the technology.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Grönvall, Erik","Fritsch, Jonas","Vallgårda, Anna"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-382932"],"event":{"acronym":"DIS","title":"ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Human Computer Interaction","Radio Signal Detection","Sensorial Augmentation","Tactile Stimuli","Wireless technology"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feltradio sensing and making sense of wireless traffic","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84978704846","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-382932","identifier":[{"id":"84978704846","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["itu-6fcced39-0691-4cd2-b71d-623b5f65d30e"],"keyword":["Human-Computer Interaction","Radio Signal Detection","Sensorial Augmentation","Tactile Stimuli","Wireless Technology"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-AE67B03C51A0B86937902EF634EDF9A8"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"gronvallpau","last":"Gronvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","name_org":"Gronvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Anna","key":"vallgårdapau","last":"Vallgårda","locid":"2fa5dc89-7d78-45d0-96c7-e8f39b78dd3e","name":"Vallgårda, Anna","orcid":"0000-0001-9898-8106","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1145/2901790.2901818","isbn":["9781450340311"],"pages":"829-840","publisher":"Association for Computing Machinery","status":"p","subtitle":"DIS '16","title":"Proceedings of the 2016 ACM Conference on Designing Interactive Systems"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84978704846"],"search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-6fcced39-0691-4cd2-b71d-623b5f65d30e"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FeltRadio: Sensing and Making Sense of Wireless Traffic","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-382932","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"author_count":3,"contributors":["Fritsch, Ester","Fritsch, Jonas"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-701231"],"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"anarchival proposals in design anthropology","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"id":"S01-000.00-701231","ids":["itu-36e495b0-aa10-4c0f-bad2-a9c7c42a8afe"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Local-1-1-5707684DB05FB79D619336C846768071"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Technologies in Practice, Technologies in Practice"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Ester","key":"fritschesterpau","last":"Fritsch","name":"Fritsch, Ester","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschjonaspau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Andrew","key":"murphieandrewpedh","last":"Murphie","name":"Murphie, Andrew","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"pages":"81-86","publisher":"The Senselab","status":"p","title":"The Go-To How-To Book of Anarchiving"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-36e495b0-aa10-4c0f-bad2-a9c7c42a8afe"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"Anarchival proposals in design anthropology","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-701231","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"FeltRadio is a portable technology for sensing WiFi through sensorial augmentation and Electric Muscle Stimulation (EMS). The technology enables its wearer to sensorially engage with the radio waves and WiFi activities that have become an integrated part of our everyday lives. The sensorial engagement changes people’s experience of WiFi activities, and allows them to participate in wireless communication infrastructures in novel ways. This is both an immediately embodied activity as it is a new form of social awareness. In this paper, we briefly present the FeltRadio technology and show how it facilitates new forms of critical reflection through sensorial participation in our contemporary experience of wireless traffic.","author_count":2,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Grönvall, Erik"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-383004"],"event":{"acronym":"COOP","end":"2016-05-27","place":"Trento, it","start":"2016-05-22","title":"COOP 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2024-06","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Critical reflection","Electric muscle stimulation","Sensorial Augmentation","Sensory Engagement","Wireless communication"],"level":"sci","mra":["sci"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"feltradio experiencing community generated wifi activities","src":["itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"http://www.springer.com/us/book/9783319334639","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-383004","ids":["itu-75c876ff-e479-4bcd-ac98-c9d5677d2baf"],"keyword":["Critical Reflection","Electric Muscle Stimulation","Sensorial Augmentation","Sensory Engagement","Wireless Communication"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Science/Technology"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3-86B33A7051CCF927C3164D708ACF5D85"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design","The Department, People and Computational Things"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"d37cba38-dff2-4c27-a515-226cfadfd849","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Erik","key":"gronvallpau","last":"Gronvall","locid":"1e0534b4-fe3e-4c5e-ad6d-5f1c7df6a14e","name":"Grönvall, Erik","name_org":"Gronvall, Erik","orcid":"0000-0002-7377-6091","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/978-3-319-33464-6_21","eisbn":["9783319334646"],"isbn":["9783319334639"],"pages":"315-321","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"COOP 2016: Proceedings of the 12th International Conference on the Design of Cooperative Systems, 23-27 May 2016, Trento, Italy"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["itu-75c876ff-e479-4bcd-ac98-c9d5677d2baf"],"src":["ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"FeltRadio – Experiencing Community-generated WiFi Activities","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-383004","year":"2016","yearsub":"2016"}
{"abstract":"This paper presents a theoretical framework for analyzing the aesthetics of participation of media architecture. The framework is based on a close reading of French philosopher Jacques Rancière and provides four points of emphasis: modes of sense perception, forms of engagement, community and emancipation. The framework is put to use in the analysis of three experimental media architectural projects; Ekkomaten/Echoes from Møllevangen, the coMotion Bench and FeltRadio. We discuss the findings from this analysis and outline future perspectives on how to develop and use the framework prospectively in the design of media architectural projects and other interactive environments.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Grönvall, Erik","Breinbjerg, Morten"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-737486"],"event":{"end":"2016-06-04","place":"Sydney, au","start":"2016-06-01","title":"Media Architecture Biennale 2016","year":"2016"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"keyword":["Aesthetics of participation","Media architecture"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"analyzing the aesthetics of participation of media architecture","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/85015397417","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-737486","identifier":[{"id":"85015397417","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a23c1023-0509-47dc-9215-0855e33b7041"],"keyword":["Aesthetics of participation","Experience philosophy","Media architecture","Politics of sensation"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-3-5-9B6E766D7FA5239E0EDB4FBD824AAC22"],"org":[{"affno":"1","country":"d