{"abstract":"The world machine is a new archetype for a socio-technical system drawing together a group of tools that combine computational powers with a social agenda of cross-world collaboration in resistance to dominant market rhetoric. Specifically, we look at how powers to connect, sense and infer can be combined and turned to crowd-sourcing public engagement with shared world issues - as an alternative to business-as-usual in the context of developing and deploying networked technology. We combine theoretical aspects of world machines, such as what a political entity of this kind might seek to do, and practical exercises that focus on design, with a view to exploring viability and examining what a related research agenda might involve.","author_count":6,"contributors":["Light, Ann","Bardzell, Jeffrey","Bardzell, Shaowen","Cox, Geoff","Fritsch, Jonas","Hansen, Lone Koefoed"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-166777"],"event":{"end":"2015-08-21","place":"Aarhus, dk","start":"2015-08-17","title":"The fifth decennial Aarhus conference","year":"2015"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"6-10 contributors","cluster_size":1,"continent":["Europe, Non-EU","OECD"],"country":["United Kingdom"],"glorg":["All Global Affiliations","University of Sussex"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"making world machines discourse design and global technologies for greater than self issues","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://ojs.statsbiblioteket.dk/index.php/ashcc/article/view/21326/18796","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-166777","ids":["au-41c9cb46-87d5-4e80-ba5f-7d4ff0dc14c0"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-3