{"author_count":5,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Iversen, Ole Sejer"],"cuid":["S01-000.00-222703"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","cluster_size":1,"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Undetermined","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"designing for experience scaffolding a design ecology","src":["au"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU"],"type":"dba","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"un","type":"url","url":"https://www.scopus.com/pages/publications/84956475513","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S01-000.00-222703","identifier":[{"id":"84956475513","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-a3e5e8d7-2b8d-42c5-b788-3a9ec7e854f2"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-1-716C9B0A383B1C410080CCED33130323"],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science","Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Participatory Information Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"beb7587a-3acb-45a3-8661-b1f5c2ed408c","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Ole Sejer","key":"iversenpau","last":"Iversen","locid":"445bdf88-e5a3-470b-ad4d-12a172f7c8a8","name":"Iversen, Ole Sejer","orcid":"0000-0002-8055-6716","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"","first":"Britta Timm","key":"knudsenpedh","last":"Knudsen","name":"Knudsen, Britta Timm","rank":3,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Dorthe Refslund","key":"christensenpedh","last":"Christensen","name":"Christensen, Dorthe Refslund","rank":4,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"},{"affno":"","first":"Per","key":"blenkerpedh","last":"Blenker","name":"Blenker, Per","rank":5,"role":"Editor of Host Publication","rolecode":"pedh"}],"pub":{"isbn":["ISBN10: 041573133X","ISBN13: 9780415731331"],"pages":"226-244","publisher":"Routledge","series":"Routledge Advances in Management and Business Studies","status":"p","subtitle":"Transforming Social Worlds","title":"Enterprising Initiatives in the Experience Economy"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-a3e5e8d7-2b8d-42c5-b788-3a9ec7e854f2"],"src":["AU Aarhus University"],"title":"Designing for experience : Scaffolding a design ecology","type":"Book Chapter","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S01-000.00-222703","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this article, we present the interactive literary installation Ink, an experimental installation displayed at the Roskilde library, and the Roskilde Festival, which is designed to prompt public reflection on the nature and role of digital literature. By manipulating three books embedded with sensors, and watching text visualized on a 55’’ screen, members of the public select from a range of predefined sentences, previously created by a Danish author, and stored in a database. Squeezing the books alters each poetic line by degrees. The final poems print onto a library receipt for their producers and upload to a blog for public viewing. We present (1) design challenges to an installation meant to persuade people to engage affectively with the ergodic nature of digital literature and (2) an in-depth analysis of the empirical findings from the installation studies at the Roskilde Festival. In particular, we highlight the broad, rich range of performative interactions facilitated by the interactive setup. This analysis examines the performative writing and reading achieved by the public through interaction with Ink and also with the resultant poems. From this exploration, we discuss general tendencies when designing affectively engaging literary interactions at the edge of art and design. Keywords: Affective engagement, Digital literature, Ergodic reading, Public displays, Performative interaction","author_count":4,"contributors":["Fritsch, Jonas","Pold, Søren Bro","Vestergaard, Lasse Steenbock","Lucas, Melissa"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-024227"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["Global Data"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Affective Interaction Design","Affective engagement","Digital Aesthetics","Digital literature","Ergodic reading","Performative interaction","Performativity","Public displays"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"Yes","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-U"],"level3":{"GTS":["DI-GTS-ALL","DI-GTS-ALX"],"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-GTS-ALX","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"ink designing for performative literary interactions","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-014-0767-2","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-024227","identifier":[{"id":"84918774696","type":"scopus"}],"ids":["au-9e287262-7955-4558-b355-3014ac0bbd9d","itu-76e12d30-46d1-4da5-b1c2-40a65e918938"],"keyword":["Affective engagement","Affective interaction design","Digital Aesthetics","Ergodic reading","Performative interaction","Performativity","digital literature","public displays"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-5-11290B8A8ADD4919BF8B16031C6E5364"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"doi","url":"https://doi.org/10.1007/s00779-014-0767-2","version":"Other Version"},{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://dx.doi.org/10.1007/s00779-014-0767-2","version":"Other Version"}],"oai":{"class":"Unused","mra":["Humanities (HUM)"],"yearPub":"2014","yearSub":"2014"},"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science","Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Participatory Information Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1},{"affno":"3","key":"alexandra institute","l2":"DI-GTS","l2n":"GTS Institutes","l3":"DI-GTS-ALX","l3nn":"Alexandra Institute","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"Alexandra Institute","namevar":["Alexandra Instituttet A/S"],"nora_code":"DI-GTS-ALX","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"beb7587a-3acb-45a3-8661-b1f5c2ed408c","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Søren Bro","key":"poldpau","last":"Pold","locid":"4db7e12a-61c5-4e14-9259-5a071cb224eb","name":"Pold, Søren Bro","orcid":"0000-0002-8924-2772","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"3","corresponding":null,"first":"Lasse Steenbock","key":"vestergaardpau","last":"Vestergaard","locid":"439c66ca-fdd2-4f15-8470-2fbbcdccc53f","name":"Vestergaard, Lasse Steenbock","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"first":"Melissa","key":"lucaspau","last":"Lucas","locid":"51e456fe-3cad-4f0c-a108-32b16cbbee12","name":"Lucas, Melissa","rank":4,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"doi":"10.1007/s00779-014-0767-2","issn":["16174909","16174917"],"issn_org":["16174909"],"issue":"7","journal":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","pages":"1551-1565","publisher":"Springer","status":"p","title":"Personal and Ubiquitous Computing","volume":"18"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","scoID":["2-s2.0-84918774696"],"search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All GTS Institutes","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-GTS","DI-GTS-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","GTS Institutes","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-9e287262-7955-4558-b355-3014ac0bbd9d","itu-76e12d30-46d1-4da5-b1c2-40a65e918938"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"INK - Designing for Performative Literary Interactions","type":"Journal Article","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-100.00-024227","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In this paper we will present a project in which we have orchestrated a collective listening process framed around the notion of the echo - and the interactive listening machine Ekkomaten – to build a participatory sound archive that reflects people’s perceptions and imaginations of a local community in the city of Aarhus Denmark. The archive is seen as indicative to the rhythm and nature of the place revealing not only aspects of the lives that unfold, but also how people sense and interpret the local community through their auditory sensibility. During the project we have asked people of all ages including children in the local youth club to collect sounds and stories from their neighbourhood by handing out a range of sound probes, containing small portable sound recorders, note books and more. The participants were encouraged to collect and notate sounds from the neighbourhood of different qualities i.e. sounds they like or dislike, sounds they find intimidating or pleasing, sounds that evoke imaginations, good or bad connotations, or sounds that represent their home, their favourite place etc. Additionally, we have collected several lengthy interviews with people who have lived in the area for many years. The sound material has been organized in an archive, whichis handled by custom build software (API), and accessible through a physical, designfictional machine called Ekkomaten. In the paper, we would like to discuss the project in relation to the following subjects: 1) Methodology: Collective listening processes and design fiction as new ways of creating and communicating urban soundscapes. 2) Critical reflection: How to engage people in reflections on the environment in which they live through their auditory sensibility. 3) Aesthetics of participation: Participation as sensation and affective modes of listening.","author_count":3,"contributors":["Breinbjerg, Morten","Fritsch, Jonas","Bertelsen, Olav W."],"cuid":["S02-092.11-013998"],"event":{"end":"2014-06-29","place":"Copenhagen, dk","start":"2014-06-27","title":"International Conference of the European Sound Studies Association","year":"2014"},"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Auditory Sensibility","Collective Listening","Design fiction","Participatory Sound Archive","Urban Soundscapes"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"pr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"in through the archive echoes from a local community","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dcp","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://essa2014.ku.dk/programme/ESSA2_program_book.pdf","version":"Other Version"},"id":"S02-092.11-013998","ids":["au-13875783-22d0-4a8a-8b62-903353f74de6","itu-4a56269f-0915-4766-98da-6f33e6c968f7"],"keyword":["Auditory Sensibility","Collective Listening","Design Fiction","Participatory Sound Archive","Urban Soundscapes"],"lang":"English","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Local-1-2-FB10D47027DE4680398D6B1CB704B03A"],"oa_link":[{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"http://essa2014.ku.dk/programme/ESSA2_program_book.pdf","version":"Other Version"}],"org":[{"affno":"1","key":"au aarhus university","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-AU","l3nl":"Aarhus University","l3nn":"AU Aarhus University","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"AU Aarhus University","namevar":["Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Centre for Advanced Visualisation and Interaction","Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Information Science","Aarhus University, Arts, School of Communication and Culture, School of Communication and Culture - Participatory Information Technology"],"nora_code":"DI-U-AU","used":1},{"affno":"2","key":"itu it university of copenhagen","l2":"DI-U","l2n":"Universities","l3":"DI-U-ITU","l3nl":"IT University of Copenhagen","l3nn":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","loc":["Denmark","Europe, EU","Nordic","OECD"],"name":"ITU IT University of Copenhagen","namevar":["IT University of Copenhagen, Business IT","IT University of Copenhagen, Digital Design"],"nora_code":"DI-U-ITU","used":1}],"person":[{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Morten","key":"breinbjergpau","last":"Breinbjerg","locid":"b02f3aab-f1ab-4748-bb16-255759b46b0d","name":"Breinbjerg, Morten","rank":1,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1 2","corresponding":null,"first":"Jonas","key":"fritschpau","last":"Fritsch","locid":"beb7587a-3acb-45a3-8661-b1f5c2ed408c","name":"Fritsch, Jonas","orcid":"0000-0001-9065-2843","rank":2,"rolecode":"pau"},{"affno":"1","corresponding":null,"country":"dk","first":"Olav W.","key":"bertelsenpau","last":"Bertelsen","locid":"bac4b6b1-9a73-4c1a-9b90-31a69af5b6b0","name":"Bertelsen, Olav W.","rank":3,"rolecode":"pau"}],"pub":{"status":"p"},"review":"Peer Reviewed","search":{"DAF":["Aarhus University","All Danish Affiliations","All Universities","DI-ALL","DI-U","DI-U-ALL","IT University of Copenhagen","Universities"],"PST":["Published"]},"sid":["au-13875783-22d0-4a8a-8b62-903353f74de6","itu-4a56269f-0915-4766-98da-6f33e6c968f7"],"src":["AU Aarhus University","ITU IT University of Copenhagen"],"title":"In through the Archive : Echoes from a local community","type":"Conference Paper","url":"https://local.forskningsportal.dk/search?modus=sin&s=LOI:S02-092.11-013998","year":"2014","yearsub":"2014"}
{"abstract":"In the introduction of Conjunction: Transdisciplinary Journal of Cultural Participation we introduce 1) the aim of the journal, 2) the journal’s conception of transdisciplinarity as an important precondition for understanding contemporary processes and dilemmas of participation, 3) important trajectories in the existing literature on participation that focus on participation as linked to technological changes, to democratic processes of transferring power, and to complex social situations calling for analytical and evaluative frameworks able to grasp multiplicity and competing interests, and 4) the theme and articles of the this special issue: cultural participation and citizenship.","author_count":5,"contributors":["Stephensen, Jan Løhmann","Reestorff, Camilla Møhring","Fabian, Louise","Fritsch, Jonas","Stage, Carsten"],"cuid":["S02-100.00-014296"],"filters":{"added":"2021-12","altsrc":["No Matches Found"],"author_count":"2-5 contributors","class":"merged","cluster_size":2,"keyword":["Cultural participation","Democracy","Multiplicity","Participatory citizenship","Power dynamics","Transdisciplinarity"],"level":"sci","mra":["hum"],"oa":"Open Access","oaiscope":"No","org":{"level1":["di"],"level2":["DI-ALL","DI-U"],"level3":{"U":["DI-U-ALL","DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"level3all":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"]},"review":"nr","rtype":["clu"],"sorti":"conjunctions introducing cultural participation as a transdisciplinary project","src":["au","itu"],"src-code":["DI-U-AU","DI-U-ITU"],"type":"dja","type-grp":["all","pub"]},"ft":{"access":"oa","type":"rem","url":"https://sciendo.com/issue/TJCP/1/1","version":"Published Version"},"id":"S02-100.00-014296","ids":["au-17af441e-ff2b-457d-a249-493f61ae040e","itu-15ffe9b0-ccf5-4136-85d1-90ba94eddaa6"],"keyword":["Cultural participation","Participatory citizenship","democracy","multiplicity","power dynamics","transdisciplinarity"],"lang":"Danish","level":"Scientific","mra":["Humanities"],"noi":["Global-Local-2-4-86709B440F9AEC07674